,"mother":"Zebudah","v":[4,5,8]},{"id":"pharaoh-nechoh_2337","name":"Pharaoh-nechoh","also":"Necho","summary":"","verses":7,"father":"","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"nebuchadnezzar_2167","name":"Nebuchadnezzar","also":"Nebuchadrezzar","summary":"In the Babylonian orthography Nabu-kudur-uzur, which means “Nebo, protect the crown!” or the “frontiers.” In an inscription he styles himself “Nebo’s favourite.”","verses":88,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6,7,10,13]},{"id":"jehoiachin_791","name":"Jehoiachin","also":"Jeconiah, Coniah, Jechonias","summary":"Succeeded his father Jehoiakin (B.C. 599) when only eight years of age, and reigned for one hundred days (2 Chr. 36:9). He is also called Jeconiah (Jer. 24:1; 27:20, etc.), and Coniah (22:24; 37:1).","verses":21,"father":"Jehoiakim","mother":"Nehushta","v":[8,9]},{"id":"zedekiah_1950","name":"Zedekiah","also":"Mattaniah","summary":"The last king of Judah. He was the third son of Josiah, and his mother’s name was Hamutal, the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah, and hence he was the brother of Jehoahaz (2 Kings 23:31; 24:17, 18).","verses":52,"father":"Josiah","mother":"Hamutal","v":[10,11]},{"id":"jeremiah_853","name":"Jeremiah","also":"Jeremy, Jeremias","summary":"One of the “greater prophets” of the Old Testament, son of Hilkiah, a priest of Anathoth (Jer. 1:1; 32:6). He was called to the prophetical office when still young (1:6), in the thirteenth year of Josiah (B.C. 628).","verses":124,"father":"Hilkiah","mother":"","v":[12,21,22]},{"id":"cyrus_968","name":"Cyrus","also":"","summary":"(Heb. Ko’resh), the celebrated “King of Persia” (Elam) who was conqueror of Babylon, and issued the decree of liberation to the Jews (Ezra 1:1, 2).","verses":19,"father":"","mother":"","v":[22,23]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” 